<svg viewBox="0 0 900 530" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Inherited terms by contract tier">
<!-- FIGURE 16.3 REQUIRED ELEMENTS
Must appear: a comparison across at least two contract tiers (standard
or self-serve terms versus enterprise terms) showing which specific terms
change between tiers (data retention, training use of customer inputs,
support responsiveness) and which remain fixed regardless of tier,
making legible that negotiation only moves specific, named terms rather
than the full agreement. Entry condition: an organization is selecting a
contract tier with a model developer. Exit condition: which terms are
negotiable at which tier is explicit rather than assumed. Deliberately
excluded: due diligence and supply chain mechanics (Figures 16.1 and
16.2's job). Must work in black and white.
SOURCE: original; the tier comparison is this chapter's own synthesis of
section 16.7's argument.
AUDIT: pass 1 [x] against list, pass 2 blind [ ], rendered and viewed [x]
-->
<title>Inherited terms by contract tier</title>
<style>
text{font-family:'Source Sans Pro','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;}
.ttl{font-size:17px;font-weight:700;}
.cls{font-size:14px;font-weight:700;}
.bx{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:400;}
.col{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;}
.sm{font-size:11px;font-weight:400;}
.em{font-size:11px;font-style:italic;}
</style>
<rect x="0" y="0" width="900" height="530" fill="#ffffff"/>
<text x="20" y="34" class="ttl" fill="#1a2230">Figure 16.3 &#183; Inherited terms by contract tier</text>
<text x="30" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">TERM</text>
<text x="430" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">STANDARD / SELF-SERVE</text>
<text x="660" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">ENTERPRISE TIER</text>
<line x1="20" y1="76" x2="880" y2="76" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.6"/>
<rect x="20" y="90" width="860" height="66" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#46536b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="114" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">Data retention</text>
<text x="32" y="132" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#46536b">NEGOTIABLE</text>
<text x="430" y="112" class="sm" fill="#46536b">provider default,</text>
<text x="430" y="128" class="sm" fill="#46536b">often extended</text>
<text x="660" y="112" class="sm" fill="#46536b">negotiated window,</text>
<text x="660" y="128" class="sm" fill="#46536b">often shortened</text>
<rect x="20" y="166" width="860" height="66" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#46536b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="190" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">Training use of customer inputs</text>
<text x="32" y="208" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#46536b">NEGOTIABLE</text>
<text x="430" y="188" class="sm" fill="#46536b">frequently permitted</text>
<text x="430" y="204" class="sm" fill="#46536b">by default</text>
<text x="660" y="188" class="sm" fill="#46536b">typically excluded</text>
<text x="660" y="204" class="sm" fill="#46536b">by contract</text>
<rect x="20" y="242" width="860" height="66" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#46536b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="266" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">Support responsiveness</text>
<text x="32" y="284" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#46536b">NEGOTIABLE</text>
<text x="430" y="264" class="sm" fill="#46536b">community or</text>
<text x="430" y="280" class="sm" fill="#46536b">best-effort</text>
<text x="660" y="264" class="sm" fill="#46536b">contracted SLA</text>
<rect x="20" y="318" width="860" height="66" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="342" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">Underlying safety and refusal calibration</text>
<text x="32" y="360" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#8794a8">FIXED</text>
<text x="430" y="340" class="sm" fill="#46536b">fixed by developer,</text>
<text x="430" y="356" class="sm" fill="#46536b">not customer-specific</text>
<text x="660" y="340" class="sm" fill="#46536b">fixed by developer,</text>
<text x="660" y="356" class="sm" fill="#46536b">not customer-specific</text>
<rect x="20" y="394" width="860" height="66" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="418" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">Usage policy prohibitions</text>
<text x="32" y="436" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#8794a8">FIXED</text>
<text x="430" y="416" class="sm" fill="#46536b">fixed by developer</text>
<text x="660" y="416" class="sm" fill="#46536b">fixed by developer</text>
<line x1="20" y1="478" x2="880" y2="478" stroke="#c9d1dc" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="20" y="496" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Enterprise tier moves the first three rows; the last two stay fixed regardless of tier or contract size,</text>
<text x="20" y="514" class="sm" fill="#46536b">since they reflect the developer's own calibration and policy rather than a commercial term.</text>
</svg>